{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01WjTQiEFsdy8D7vCHkJaT7B","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t# 03: Seat selection, legend and selected-seats panel\n2\t\n3\t**What to build:** On the seat map the customer selects and deselects seats and couches, up to 10 seats per booking with a couch counting as 2. Unavailable seats cannot be selected. Exceeding the limit shows a toast. Every state has its colour, the legend explains them, and the selected-seats panel lists the current selection by row.\n4\t\n5\t**Specification:** sections 3.2, 5.2, 5.3, 5.5, 9.2, 9.6, 9.7.\n6\t\n7\t**Blocked by:** 02 — Auditorium map.\n8\t\n9\t**Status:** ready\n10\t\n11\t- [ ] AC-16 — Seats listed in `occupiedSeats` for the screening are rendered unavailable and cannot be selected.\n12\t- [ ] AC-17 — A couch is unavailable when either of its two seat identifiers is in `occupiedSeats`.\n13\t- [ ] AC-18 — Clicking an available seat selects it; clicking it again deselects it.\n14\t- [ ] AC-19 — Clicking a couch selects both of its seats as one unit; it cannot be half-selected.\n15\t- [ ] AC-20 — Selection is capped at 10 seats; a couch counts as 2.\n16\t- [ ] AC-21 — A click that would exceed 10 seats is ignored and shows the toast `Maximum 10 seats per booking`.\n17\t- [ ] AC-22 — At the cap, already selected seats and couches can still be deselected.\n18\t- [ ] AC-23 — The legend lists exactly `Available`, `Selected`, `Unavailable`, `Accessible`.\n19\t- [ ] AC-24 — Available seats use `#2E7D32`.\n20\t- [ ] AC-25 — Selected seats use `#F9A825`.\n21\t- [ ] AC-26 — Unavailable seats use `#C62828`.\n22\t- [ ] AC-27 — Accessible seats use `#1565C0`.\n23\t- [ ] AC-58 — Between the seat map and the `Cancel` / `Continue` buttons, the selected-seats panel shows `Selected seats: <n>` and one `Row <r>: <seats>` line per row, updated on every selection change.\n24\t- [ ] AC-66 — Every seat-selection identifier in section 9.2, and the toast identifier in section 9.6, is 