{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user's sole explicit request (given at the start of the conversation) was:\n   \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n\n   No further user messages were received after this. All subsequent work has been autonomous implementation and verification against this single directive. Key constraints embedded in the spec that must be honored throughout:\n   - Package manager is pnpm only (never npm/yarn).\n   - App must be served at http://localhost:4200 — port must not change.\n   - No new dependencies may be added; everything needed is already installed (MUI 9, MUI X Date Pickers, dayjs, React Router 6, etc.).\n   - Never hand-edit db.json.\n   - Desktop-only (viewport ≥1280×720), all text in English.\n   - Section 9's data-testid contract is exact and must not be renamed/abbreviated/prefixed/misplaced.\n   - Do not change db.json or date logic just to make screenings visible under the real current date — a \"No screenings on this day\" empty state for all reachable dates is expected and correct given db.json's Sept 2026 dates vs. the sandbox's real date of Oct 15, 2026.\n   - Out-of-scope items (section 11) must NOT be built: user accounts, real payments, seat locking, occupiedSeats mutation, posters/images, responsive/mobile layouts, keyboard nav/ARIA beyond defaults, translations.\n   - Task is only \"finished\" when every ticket (01–07) is done AND `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Nx 23 monorepo, Vite build system (esbuild-based, does NOT type-check by default — only `tsc --noEmit` via `nx typecheck` catches real TS errors), React 19, React Router 6 (`BrowserRouter`, `Routes`/`Route`, `Navigate`, `useParams`, `useNavigate`, `useSearchParams`).\n   - MUI 9 (`@mui/material`) with the newer `slots`/`slotProps` API (not legacy `InputLabelProps`/`InputProps`), MUI X Date Pickers 9.14.0 (`DatePicker` from `@mui/x-date-pickers/DatePicker`), dayjs for date formatting/parsing.\n   - CSS Modules (`*.module.scss`) used throughout for component-scoped styling (no global class collisions), matching tsconfig's `@nx/react/typings/cssmodule.d.ts` typing support.\n   - sessionStorage-backed booking state machine with strict lifecycle rules (section 3.1 of spec): booking holds screeningId, selected seats, checkout form values, paid flag, and customer email once paid; route guards must snapshot their \"allowed\" check once at mount (route entry / reload) rather than reactively, per spec's explicit requirement that in-page state changes (e.g., removing the last summary item) must not trigger a guard redirect.\n   - Seat/couch domain modeling: seat identifiers `R<row>C<col>`; couches occupy two adjacent column identifiers and are toggled/priced/described as a single atomic unit; accessible seats (row 1, cols 10–15) use the same price as the rest of row 1 but a distinct color when free & unselected.\n   - Toast system: single-toast-at-a-time, 4-second auto-dismiss, implemented via MUI `Snackbar`/`SnackbarContent`.\n   - Checkout form validation: field-level touched-state (local component state, NOT persisted) gating when error messages display, full email regex per spec's exact definition, confirm-email cross-field validation re-evaluated live.\n   - TypeScript type-safety gaps discovered: Vite's production build (esbuild) does not catch type errors that `tsc --noEmit` (the `typecheck` Nx target) does — both must be run to be confident of correctness.\n   - `CI=true` environment variable required to avoid pnpm's interactive \"Aborted removal of modules directory due to no TTY\" prompt when running Nx targets in this sandboxed environment.\n   - `curl` is NOT installed in this sandbox; `node -e \"fetch(...)\"` was used as a substitute, though it unexpectedly also failed with ECONNREFUSED against servers that appeared (per their logs) to have started successfully — likely due to background subshell process lifecycle issues with `(cmd &)` syntax.\n   - `run` skill / `chromium-cli` pattern for browser-driven verification: start dev servers, poll until ready, then pipe `nav`/`wait-for`/`click`/`fill`/`screenshot`/`console --errors` commands to a `chromium-cli --session <name>` REPL via stdin.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections (all under `/workspace/project/apps/cinescope/src/` unless noted):\n\n   - **`api/types.ts`** (created): `Movie`, `Screening`, `ReservationCustomer`, `Reservation`, `CreateReservationPayload` interfaces mirroring spec section 2.1 exactly.\n\n   - **`api/client.ts`** (created): Thin fetch wrapper against `BASE_URL = 'http://localhost:3000'`; exports `fetchMovies()`, `fetchScreenings()`, `fetchScreening(id)`, `fetchMovie(id)`, `createReservation(payload)`. Non-2xx responses throw.\n\n   - **`seating/layout.ts`** (created): Geometry/pricing constants and helpers — `ROW_COUNT=15`, `COLUMN_COUNT=24`, `COUCH_ROW=15`, `MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING=10`, `range(start,end)`, `isAccessibleSeat(row,col)`, `priceForRow(row)`, `getRowBlocks(row)` (returns `{left, middle, right}` column arrays; `left` empty for rows 1–10 as the entrance), `toCouchPairs(cols)`, `seatId(row,col)`.\n\n   - **`seating/units.ts`** (created): `Unit` union (`SingleSeatUnit | CouchUnit`), `parseSeatId`, `unitColumn`, `unitsFromSeats(seats: string[])` (groups seat ids by row, pairs row-15 ids into couches, sorts by row then column), `unitIds`, `unitSeatCount`, `unitPrice`, `unitSeatDescription`, `unitCouchLabel`, `couchIds`, `formatPrice(amount)`.\n\n   - **`seating/state.ts`** (created): `SeatState` type, `SEAT_STATE_COLORS` map (`#2E7D32` available, `#F9A825` selected, `#C62828` unavailable, `#1565C0` accessible), `computeSeatState(isAccessible, isOccupied, isSelected)`, `computeCouchState(isOccupied, isSelected)` (couches never return 'accessible').\n\n   - **`utils/date.ts`** (created): `ISO_DATE_FORMAT`, `today()`, `parseIsoDate(value)` (strict dayjs parse, null on invalid), `formatShowDate(date,time)` → `dddd D MMM HH:mm` format (e.g. \"Tuesday 15 Sep 16:00\").\n\n   - **`toast/ToastContext.tsx`** (created): `ToastProvider` + `useToast()`. Uses MUI `Snackbar` + `SnackbarContent` with `data-testid=\"toast\"`; `showToast(message)` clears any pending timeout, sets message, and schedules clearing after 4000ms.\n\n   - **`booking/types.ts`** (created): `CheckoutFormValues`, `Booking`, `EMPTY_FORM_VALUES`, `createEmptyBooking(screeningId)`.\n\n   - **`booking/storage.ts`** (created): `loadBooking()`/`saveBooking()` against `sessionStorage` key `'cinescope.booking'`.\n\n   - **`booking/BookingContext.tsx`** (created): `BookingProvider` (wraps children, must be rendered under `ToastProvider` since it calls `useToast()` internally) and `useBooking()` hook exposing `{ booking, initForScreening, toggleUnit, removeUnit, setFormField, markPaid, clear }`. Key logic:\n     ```tsx\n     const initForScreening = useCallback((screeningId: number) => {\n       setBooking((prev) => {\n         if (prev && prev.screeningId === screeningId && !prev.paid) {\n           return prev;\n         }\n         return createEmptyBooking(screeningId);\n       });\n     }, []);\n\n     const toggleUnit = useCallback((ids: string[]) => {\n       setBooking((prev) => {\n         if (!prev) return prev;\n         const allSelected = ids.every((id) => prev.seats.includes(id));\n         if (allSelected) {\n           return { ...prev, seats: prev.seats.filter((id) => !ids.includes(id)) };\n         }\n         if (prev.seats.length + ids.length > MAX_SEATS_PER_BOOKING) {\n           showToast('Maximum 10 seats per booking');\n           return prev;\n         }\n         return { ...prev, seats: [...prev.seats, ...ids] };\n       });\n     }, [showToast]);\n     ```\n\n   - **`booking/useBookingGuard.ts`** (created): \n     ```ts\n     export function useBookingGuard(predicate: () => boolean): boolean {\n       const [allowed] = useState(predicate);\n       return allowed;\n     }\n     ```\n     Captures the guard result once at mount so later in-page booking mutations don't trigger a redirect — this directly implements the spec's requirement that guard checks \"run when a route is entered... not while the customer stays on a screen.\"\n\n   - **`components/DayPicker/DayPicker.tsx`** (created, then edited): Renders `day-picker` container, `day-button`s (with `data-date`, `data-selected`), and a wrapped `DatePicker` with `data-testid=\"date-picker\"`. **Edit history**: originally used MUI `<Stack direction=\"row\" spacing={2} alignItems=\"center\">`, which failed `tsc` typecheck (\"Property 'alignItems' does not exist...\"); replaced with a plain `<div className={styles.container}>` (flexbox via new `DayPicker.module.scss`). Also originally tried `slotProps={{ textField: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker', size: 'small' } }}` on the `DatePicker`, which failed typecheck (`PickersTextFieldProps` doesn't accept `data-testid` in that slot type); fixed by wrapping `<DatePicker>` in a plain `<div data-testid=\"date-picker\">` and keeping only `slotProps={{ textField: { size: 'small' } }}`.\n\n   - **`components/DayPicker/DayPicker.module.scss`** (created): simple flexbox container styles.\n\n   - **`components/AuditoriumMap/AuditoriumMap.tsx`** (created): Renders `screen-indicator` + `seat-map` with 15 rows (`seat-row`, `row-label-left`/`row-label-right`, `aisle` ×2 per row, left/middle/right blocks sized via `blockSmall`(124px)/`blockLarge`(508px) CSS classes for consistent column alignment across rows regardless of entrance gaps; row 15 renders `Couch` components instead of `Seat`).\n\n   - **`components/AuditoriumMap/AuditoriumMap.module.scss`**, **`Seat.tsx`**, **`Couch.tsx`** (created): Seat/Couch are plain `<button>` elements with `data-testid=\"seat\"`/`\"couch\"`, `data-row`, `data-column`/`data-column-start`+`data-column-end`, `data-state`, `disabled` when unavailable, background color set inline from `SEAT_STATE_COLORS`.\n\n   - **`components/Legend/Legend.tsx`** and **`.module.scss`** (created): renders 4 `legend-item`s (Available/Selected/Unavailable/Accessible) with color swatches.\n\n   - **`components/SelectedSeatsPanel/SelectedSeatsPanel.tsx`** (created): renders `selected-seats-count` (`Selected seats: <n>`) and one `selected-seats-row` per occupied row, grouped/sorted via `unitsFromSeats`.\n\n   - **`pages/MovieListPage/MovieListPage.tsx`** and **`.module.scss`** (created): Fetches `fetchMovies()`+`fetchScreenings()` once on mount (and on Retry), filters client-side by the URL's `?date=` param (defaulting to today when missing/invalid/past), renders day picker + loading/error/empty/loaded movie-card list states with all required data-testids (`movies-loading`, `movies-error`, `movies-retry-button`, `movies-empty`, `movie-list`, `movie-card`, `movie-title`, `movie-genre`, `movie-runtime`, `movie-format`, `screening-button`).\n\n   - **`pages/SeatSelectionPage/SeatSelectionPage.tsx`** and **`.module.scss`** (created): Loads screening+movie via effect; on failure `navigate('/', {replace:true})`; on success calls `initForScreening(screeningId)` once (tracked via `initedRef`); renders `seat-map-title`, `seat-map-subtitle`, `seat-limit-info`, `AuditoriumMap`, `Legend`, `SelectedSeatsPanel`, `cancel-button` (clears booking, navigates to `/`), `continue-button` (disabled when no seats selected, navigates to summary).\n\n   - **`pages/SummaryPage/SummaryPage.tsx`** and **`.module.scss`** (created): Uses `useBookingGuard` (unpaid + matching screeningId + ≥1 seat), loads screening+movie, renders `summary-title`, `summary-list` of `summary-item`s (title/datetime/row/seat/price/remove-button), `summary-total`, `back-button`, `confirm-button`. Removing the last item navigates back to the seat map.\n\n   - **`pages/CheckoutPage/validation.ts`** (created): Pure validation functions per spec section 7's exact rules and messages, including the email regex `/^[^\\s@]+@[^\\s@]+\\.[^\\s@]+$/` (verified by hand against spec's \"not-an-email\", \"a@b\", \"a@.com\" invalid examples and \"anna@example.com\" valid example).\n\n   - **`pages/CheckoutPage/CheckoutPage.tsx`** and **`.module.scss`** (created, then edited for lint cleanliness): Full form with local `touched` state (not persisted) and values bound directly to `booking.formValues` (persisted via `setFormField`). Pay button toggles between `Pay <total> PLN` and `Processing…`. On invalid submit: marks all fields touched, shows toast `'The form contains errors'`, no navigation. On valid submit: `createReservation(...)` → success calls `markPaid(email)` and navigates to `/confirmation`; failure shows toast `'Payment failed. Please try again.'` and re-enables the button. **Edit history**: initially used `slotProps={{ inputLabel: { 'data-testid': '...' } as any }}` on each `TextField` (5 occurrences) to attach `-label` testids — this passed `tsc` but produced 5 ESLint `@typescript-eslint/no-explicit-any` warnings. Fixed by adding:\n     ```ts\n     import { InputLabelProps } from '@mui/material/InputLabel';\n     function labelSlotProps(testId: string): InputLabelProps {\n       return { 'data-testid': testId } as InputLabelProps;\n     }\n     ```\n     and replacing all 5 usages with `slotProps={{ inputLabel: labelSlotProps('first-name-label') }}` (and similarly for last-name/email/confirm-email/phone), via a `sed` command. Also fixed a separate unused-`movie`-variable warning in `SeatSelectionPage.tsx` by changing `const { screening, movie } = state;` to `const { screening } = state;`.\n\n   - **`pages/ConfirmationPage/ConfirmationPage.tsx`** (created): Uses `useBookingGuard(() => !!booking && booking.paid)`; renders `confirmation-heading`, `confirmation-message` (with `booking.customerEmail`), `confirmation-continue-button` (clears booking, navigates to `/`).\n\n   - **`app/app.tsx`** (edited): Replaced the scaffold's bare `<Routes />` with:\n     ```tsx\n     export function App() {\n       return (\n         <ToastProvider>\n           <BookingProvider>\n             <Routes>\n               <Route path=\"/\" element={<MovieListPage />} />\n               <Route path=\"/screenings/:id/seats\" element={<SeatSelectionPage />} />\n               <Route path=\"/screenings/:id/summary\" element={<SummaryPage />} />\n               <Route path=\"/screenings/:id/checkout\" element={<CheckoutPage />} />\n               <Route path=\"/confirmation\" element={<ConfirmationPage />} />\n               <Route path=\"*\" element={<Navigate to=\"/\" replace />} />\n             </Routes>\n           </BookingProvider>\n         </ToastProvider>\n       );\n     }\n     ```\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n   - **pnpm interactive prompt**: `pnpm nx build cinescope` initially failed with `[ERR_PNPM_ABORTED_REMOVE_MODULES_DIR_NO_TTY]`. Fixed by prefixing all Nx commands with `CI=true` (e.g., `CI=true pnpm nx build cinescope`), which allowed pnpm to recreate `node_modules` non-interactively; build then succeeded (output chunk ~690KB, with a \"chunk larger than 500kB\" warning which is informational only, not an error).\n   - **MUI `Stack` typecheck error** in `DayPicker.tsx`: `<Stack direction=\"row\" spacing={2} alignItems=\"center\" data-testid=\"day-picker\">` failed `tsc --noEmit -p tsconfig.app.json` with \"No overload matches this call... Property 'alignItems' does not exist on type...\". Fixed by removing the `Stack` import/usage entirely and replacing with a plain `<div className={styles.container}>` using new flexbox CSS in `DayPicker.module.scss`.\n   - **MUI X `DatePicker` slotProps typecheck error**: `slotProps={{ textField: { 'data-testid': 'date-picker', size: 'small' } }}` failed with \"Object literal may only specify known properties, and ''data-testid'' does not exist in type 'SlotComponentPropsFromProps<PickersTextFieldProps,...>'\". Fixed by wrapping the `<DatePicker>` in `<div data-testid=\"date-picker\">` and removing `data-testid` from `slotProps.textField` (kept only `size: 'small'`).\n   - Re-ran `pnpm nx typecheck cinescope` after both fixes — passed with 0 errors.\n   - **ESLint warnings** (not errors, build/lint both still \"succeeded\" overall): 5× `no-explicit-any` in `CheckoutPage.tsx` from `as any` casts on `slotProps.inputLabel`; 1× `no-unused-vars` for `movie` in `SeatSelectionPage.tsx`. Both fixed as described in section 3 above (typed `labelSlotProps` helper; removed unused destructure). Re-ran lint — 0 problems. Re-ran typecheck — 0 errors. Re-ran build — succeeded again (output: `index.html` 0.65kB, css 2.28kB, js 690.30kB).\n   - **`curl` not found**: Attempting `timeout 40 bash -c 'until curl -sf ... ; do sleep 1; done'` failed repeatedly with `bash: line 1: curl: command not found` for both the API (port 3000) and app (port 4200) readiness checks, looping for the full 40s and exiting with code 124 (timeout). This tool is simply unavailable in this sandbox.\n   - **Background server logs looked healthy but `node -e \"fetch(...)\"` got `ECONNREFUSED`**: After confirming via `cat /tmp/api.log` and `cat /tmp/serve.log` that json-server (port 3000) and Vite (port 4200) had both started successfully (\"Watching...\" and \"Local: http://localhost:4200/\" respectively), I substituted `node -e \"fetch('http://localhost:3000/movies')...\"` and `node -e \"fetch('http://localhost:4200')...\"` for connectivity checks (since `curl`/`wget` weren't confirmed available). Both calls failed with `ECONNREFUSED` (`connect ECONNREFUSED 127.0.0.1:3000` / `:4200`). **This was not yet diagnosed or resolved** when the conversation was cut off for summary — the likely cause is that the servers were started via `(pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &) && (CI=true pnpm nx serve cinescope > /tmp/serve.log 2>&1 &)`, where each `(cmd &)` runs in its own subshell that exits immediately after backgrounding the job; depending on the sandbox's process/session handling, this can let the backgrounded child get reaped or orphaned once the enclosing subshell exits, even though its earlier startup log lines were captured before that happened.\n\n5. Problem Solving:\n   - Solved: Full architecture and implementation of the booking lifecycle (sessionStorage-backed, with precise \"keep vs. reset\" and route-guard semantics matching spec section 3.1), the auditorium geometry/pricing/coloring system, the full checkout validation flow with touched-state semantics, and all required `data-testid`/data-attribute contracts per spec section 9 — all implemented and passing `pnpm nx build cinescope`, `pnpm nx typecheck cinescope`, and `pnpm nx lint cinescope` cleanly.\n   - Solved: Reasoned carefully through subtle spec details to avoid under/over-engineering, e.g.:\n     - Verified the email regex against all four spec examples by hand.\n     - Verified couch/seat counts add up to 308 selectable elements (200 rows1-10 + 96 rows11-14 + 12 couches row15) and that block widths (124px small block / 508px large block) stay visually/structurally consistent whether populated by seats or couches or left empty as the entrance.\n     - Chose to fetch all movies+screenings once per page-open and filter client-side by date (rather than refetching per day-button click), since spec says \"loaded... each time the screen opens\" and AC-53 only requires correct filtering, not a request-per-day.\n     - Designed the guard hook (`useBookingGuard`) specifically to snapshot once at mount, directly satisfying the spec's explicit \"these checks run when a route is entered... not while the customer stays on a screen\" requirement — this was a deliberate architectural choice, not incidental.\n   - Ongoing/unresolved at cutoff: Verifying the running app behaves correctly end-to-end via browser automation. The dev servers were started in the background but the most recent connectivity check (`node -e fetch`) failed with ECONNREFUSED for both ports, despite log files showing successful startup messages. This needs to be re-diagnosed (e.g., restart servers without wrapping each in its own throwaway subshell, confirm the processes are still alive with `ps`/`jobs`, and retry readiness polling) before proceeding with chromium-cli-driven UI verification.\n\n6. All user messages:\n   - The single, complete, initial user instruction: \"Build the cinema seat-booking web application described in spec/README.md, as the React application already set up in this Nx workspace (Nx project `cinescope` in apps/cinescope); its stack is described in spec/stack.md. The work is split into tickets in spec/tickets/; implement them in order. spec/README.md is the complete specification: do not ask any questions, and where it is silent choose the simplest option that satisfies it. Finish only when every ticket is done and `pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\"\n   - No other user-role messages occurred in this conversation. (The final message in the transcript is a system-level directive, not from the user, instructing a tool-free summary response.)\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n   - Complete manual/automated verification that the running application (backend `pnpm api` on :3000, frontend `pnpm nx serve cinescope` on :4200) actually behaves correctly end-to-end: movie list (loading/error/empty/loaded states, day picker, screening navigation), seat selection (geometry, selection/deselection, 10-seat cap + toast, legend, colors, selected-seats panel), summary (listing, remove, total, back/confirm), checkout (field validation messages, touched-state timing, pay button states, POST /reservations success/failure toasts), and confirmation (message with email, Continue clearing booking) — ideally via `chromium-cli` screenshots as initially planned, checking `console --errors` for runtime issues not caught by build/typecheck/lint.\n   - Work through ticket 07 (\"Final pass\"): \"A walk through the whole flow — movie list, seat map, summary, checkout, confirmation — against the specification, fixing whatever does not match,\" with its two checklist items: \"Every acceptance criterion in section 10 is met\" and \"`pnpm nx build cinescope` succeeds.\" This requires explicitly re-checking each AC-01 through AC-69 against the implementation (not yet done systematically — only build/typecheck/lint have been verified so far).\n   - Mark/confirm the tickets' checkboxes conceptually complete (the ticket files themselves are spec/reference documents with `- [ ]` boxes; whether they need to be physically ticked in the markdown files was not addressed — likely not required since they are specification artifacts, but worth a final judgment call).\n   - Re-verify the booking lifecycle edge cases live in-browser: reload persistence on seat map/summary/checkout/confirmation, \"Cancel\" and \"Continue\" clearing the booking, starting a new booking when opening a seat map for a different/already-paid screening, and that checkout values survive Back-then-Forward and reload but a brand-new booking starts with an empty form (AC-64).\n   - Since all screenings in db.json fall in Sept 2026 (before the sandbox's real \"today\" of Oct 15, 2026) and the datepicker disables past dates, verification of the seat map/summary/checkout/confirmation flow must be done via direct navigation to a screening URL (e.g., `http://localhost:4200/screenings/1/seats`) rather than through the movie list's day picker.\n\n8. Current Work:\n   Immediately before the summary request, I was in the middle of the **manual verification phase** using the `run` skill's browser-driven pattern. Specifically, I had:\n   1. Invoked the `run` skill with instructions to start both servers and verify movie list / seat selection / summary / checkout validation / payment / confirmation via chromium-cli screenshots, explicitly noting the date mismatch caveat (today = 2026-10-15, screenings dated 2026-09-15 to 2026-09-21, so navigate directly to `/screenings/1/seats` rather than relying on the day picker).\n   2. Per the skill's guidance, started both dev servers in the background:\n      ```bash\n      cd /workspace/project && (pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 &) && (CI=true pnpm nx serve cinescope > /tmp/serve.log 2>&1 &) && sleep 1 && echo started\n      ```\n   3. Attempted to poll for readiness with `curl` in `until` loops — failed outright because `curl` is not installed in this sandbox (`curl: command not found`, looping for the full 40s timeout).\n   4. Checked the log files directly (`cat /tmp/api.log`, `cat /tmp/serve.log`), which showed both servers reporting successful startup (json-server \"Watching...\" on port 3000; Vite \"ready in 168ms... Local: http://localhost:4200/\").\n   5. As a substitute connectivity check, ran `node -e \"fetch('http://localhost:3000/movies')...\"` and `node -e \"fetch('http://localhost:4200')...\"`, both of which unexpectedly returned `ECONNREFUSED` errors — this contradicts the log files' apparent success and has not yet been explained or resolved.\n\n   This was the exact point at which the conversation was interrupted for a mandatory summary; no diagnosis or fix for the ECONNREFUSED issue has been attempted yet.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\n   Re-diagnose and fix the server connectivity issue, then resume the browser-driven verification exactly as planned. Concretely, the next step is to confirm whether the background server processes are actually still alive (e.g., via `ps aux | grep -E \"json-server|vite\"` or `jobs -l`), and if they were killed when their wrapping `(cmd &)` subshells exited, restart them using a backgrounding approach that survives the subshell exit (e.g., `nohup pnpm api > /tmp/api.log 2>&1 & disown` and `nohup env CI=true pnpm nx serve cinescope > /tmp/serve.log 2>&1 & disown`, or using `run_in_background: true` on the Bash tool as intended for long-running background processes), then retry the readiness poll against both ports before continuing with the `chromium-cli` driven verification of the movie list, seat selection, summary, checkout, and confirmation screens as described in my message to the `run` skill: \"Start the cinescope app (pnpm api for backend on :3000, pnpm nx serve cinescope for frontend on :4200) and verify key screens work: the movie list at /, direct navigation to /screenings/1/seats for seat selection, selecting seats, continuing to summary, checkout form validation, and submitting payment to reach /confirmation.\"\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /capture/claude-config/projects/-workspace-project/b57fd512-3185-49f1-a3f5-4ca4529fa7ab.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b57fd512-3185-49f1-a3f5-4ca4529fa7ab","uuid":"378b4c5b-c01e-4069-b1c0-659f542e69d1","timestamp":"2026-10-15T08:59:59.718Z","isSynthetic":true}
